  "cover_text": "Residential buildings account for a significant amount of the national budget and annually spend into the billions; the scale of the problem that has not been properly addressed includes congestion, the waste of unnecessary resources and waste of indivisible demand for water, gas and electricity, as well as historic urban centre consolidation. On this basis there have been recommendations in the last 5 years to have a green growth strategy embodied in the local theme and be brought to the forefront of planning strategies.\nDuring my visit to Czechia I had the chance to meet with Cristina Sikorska and her team to find out about the way in which the long-standing relationship between sustainable city planning and parks and recreational spaces has been supported by the government. Particular attention will be given to scoring results both on the buildings and benches that are the focal points of the environment, whether in public spaces in Bucharest or Plzeň.\nThe Pedigree Lecture is a series of one hour public lectures designed for professionals and anyone involved in the field of urban synthesis who wishes to better",
